  "lineage_differences": [
    "M64K adds native B and Q inputs, exact 128-bit Q widening multiply, and 128-by-64 wide divide.",
    "M64K uses unified GPR operands and has no implicit memory operand.",
    "M64K makes condition-state writes explicit through .F and always preserves X.",
    "M64K reports quotient overflow as a precise synchronous fault instead of a V-only non-write result.",
    "M64K divide faults save the faulting PC in native CSR trap state rather than using Motorola vector frames or next-PC trap semantics.",
    "M64K provides explicit quotient-only, remainder-only, fused quotient-remainder, and double-width-dividend forms as single architectural operations."
